                    {
                        "form_id": "2c066ee7-1381-4d20-bc94-b8c7fc3babdc",
                        "entry_id": "7525a52e-ae21-3e5e-a73d-02934fefb48b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "multiculturelles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "935390c2-7e4f-30d5-959d-f9feb0100523",
                        "entry_id": "7525a52e-ae21-3e5e-a73d-02934fefb48b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui concerne plusieurs cultures, qui a rapport avec plusieurs cultures."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c64104e1-0a7a-323a-b66b-bf8d4036e2a1",
                        "entry_id": "7525a52e-ae21-3e5e-a73d-02934fefb48b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est caractérisé par la présence importante de plusieurs cultures qui se côtoient."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Moderne"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "752df8dc-d1d8-445e-bef0-4b162d3b0f54",
                                "sense_id": "c64104e1-0a7a-323a-b66b-bf8d4036e2a1",
                                "text": "Il va sans dire que l’idée du Canada comme nation multiculturelle a suscité la grogne de quelques groupes, au premier chef les nationalistes québécois, promoteurs d’une vision du Canada comme État multinational qui ne s'assume pas, ou comme pays incapable de surmonter et de « gérer » la réalité de ses deux groupes fondateurs, réalité qui renvoie à la domination historique de la minorité francophone par la majorité anglophone, donnée indépassable sans la reconnaissance du Québec comme nation à part entière – on connaît le récit…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a45b3686-fb95-4566-b91e-5abecc063713",
                                "sense_id": "c64104e1-0a7a-323a-b66b-bf8d4036e2a1",
                                "text": "Molenbeek est aussi une ville multiculturelle, où plus d’un quart de la population est de nationalité étrangère."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "032c8c4f-c9d4-48d9-9de4-bae9fe4e0b58",
                        "source_entry_id": "7525a52e-ae21-3e5e-a73d-02934fefb48b",
                        "target_lang_word": "multikulturell",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "multikulturell",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1dcf0928-ea68-38f5-82e4-4cbf702ad3dd",
                                        "entry_id": "2a894ff2-92a6-364d-ac5c-88bfdd14484a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "von mehreren unterschiedlichen Kulturen geprägt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb3caa03-f610-4d3c-8e8d-2de98c625aec",
                                                "sense_id": "1dcf0928-ea68-38f5-82e4-4cbf702ad3dd",
                                                "text": "Multikulturell ist zur Zeit ein Schlüsselbegriff in der politischen Auseinandersetzung darüber, ob beziehungsweise wieweit sich unsere Gesellschaft anderen Kulturen, die Immigranten mitbringen, öffnen soll."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc65418b-296b-4a74-9541-89deb7f3de02",
                                                "sense_id": "1dcf0928-ea68-38f5-82e4-4cbf702ad3dd",
                                                "text": "Zu unserem multikulturellen Stadtteilfest reisen zahlreiche Künstler an."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f842da95-41ec-43e2-ac34-e5e8418e9c37",
                        "source_entry_id": "7525a52e-ae21-3e5e-a73d-02934fefb48b",
                        "target_lang_word": "multicultural",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "multicultural",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed5af85b-32ae-3107-a1db-0f01d8cece5a",
                                        "entry_id": "a711c7e4-3a9e-364f-8f6c-a1e3f848bfb2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating or pertaining to several different cultures."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33c0fe32-9fa6-445b-9d03-59b35afa49a1",
                                                "sense_id": "ed5af85b-32ae-3107-a1db-0f01d8cece5a",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: polycultural (several or many)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8255db7d-c8d2-4d4e-8cf8-4b93bdd812d3",
                                                "sense_id": "ed5af85b-32ae-3107-a1db-0f01d8cece5a",
                                                "text": "Viewed from the boardrooms of Britain, the market is becoming more multicultural than could have been imagined just five years ago."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c475a85f-612b-4bee-82bf-02bdc8f8dda7",
                                                "sense_id": "ed5af85b-32ae-3107-a1db-0f01d8cece5a",
                                                "text": "The literary landscape of London is as varied as the city itself. According to the 2011 census, 40 percent of residents identified as “Asian, Black, Mixed or Other.” While this is no multi-culti utopia, it is undeniably an intensely multicultural metropolis where more than 300 languages are spoken."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aac108fd-bfe9-394a-b720-774c7a03be53",
                                        "entry_id": "a711c7e4-3a9e-364f-8f6c-a1e3f848bfb2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating or pertaining to groups, households or families involving persons with different or mixed ethnicities or races."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "euphemistic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81ef3739-acb3-4cc8-9e62-19aa6d6f5a50",
                                                "sense_id": "aac108fd-bfe9-394a-b720-774c7a03be53",
                                                "text": "Bedgood, whose father is African American and mother is Caucasian, says he's struggling to deal with such hatred. He grew up in Santa Clarita and says he could not have imagined something like this happening in a quiet community with many multicultural families."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
